Dataset
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The models distributed with this work are trained on the autoPET whole-body
PET/CT lesion databases. The imaging data is NOT redistributed here; it must be
obtained from the sources below, under their terms.

   A whole-body FDG-PET/CT dataset with manually annotated tumor lesions
   (FDG-PET-CT-Lesions)
   Gatidis S, Kuestner T.  The Cancer Imaging Archive, 2022.
   DICOM (TCIA):   https://doi.org/10.7937/gkr0-xv29
   NIfTI (FDAT):   https://doi.org/10.57754/FDAT.8f14a-pf846
   Paper:          https://doi.org/10.1038/s41597-022-01718-3

   A whole-body PSMA-PET/CT dataset with manually annotated tumor lesions
   (PSMA-PET-CT-Lesions), Version 1
   Jeblick K, et al.  The Cancer Imaging Archive, 2024.
   DICOM (TCIA):   https://doi.org/10.7937/r7ep-3x37
   NIfTI (FDAT):   https://doi.org/10.57754/FDAT.g27kx-86t35

   The cohort actually used here is the organisers' combined FDG + PSMA release of
   these two databases, 1611 cases:
   NIfTI (FDAT):   https://doi.org/10.57754/FDAT.rdkqd-wdh87

   The prompt heatmaps that form input channels 2 and 3 are published by the
   organisers in the challenge repository, as nnunet-baseline/heatmaps.zip:
   https://github.com/lab-midas/autoPETV

   Both databases are dual-licensed by their creators: the DICOM form under the
   TCIA Restricted License, which requires a signed license agreement before
   access, and the NIfTI form under the Creative Commons Attribution-
   NonCommercial 4.0 International licence (CC BY-NC 4.0),
   https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc/4.0/

   CC BY-NC 4.0 permits non-commercial use with attribution, and this section is
   that attribution. It is not a permissive licence, and it differs from the
   Apache 2.0 licence covering the source code in this repository: the licence
   on the code grants nothing over the data. The organisers ask to be contacted
   before the databases are used in a commercial setting (https://autopet.org).

   Two files tracked in this repository are keyed on the databases' case
   identifiers, and are derived from them rather than authored here:

     splits/fold_*.csv               the five-fold case assignment, which
                                     originates in the splits_final.json
                                     distributed alongside the data

     assets/preprocessing/ref.json   one PET reference value per case, computed
                                     from that case's own voxels by
                                     preprocessing/reference.py

   Neither holds image data and neither can reconstruct any. They are recorded
   here so their origin is on the record.

