Model weights
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Training initialises from the per-fold checkpoints of:

   autoPET III LesionTracer
   Rokuss, Maximilian -- German Cancer Research Center (DKFZ)
   Published 2024-09-15 via Zenodo: https://zenodo.org/records/14007247
   Code: https://github.com/MIC-DKFZ/autopet-3-submission
   Paper: "From FDG to PSMA: A Hitchhiker's Guide to Multitracer, Multicenter
          Lesion Segmentation in PET/CT Imaging", arXiv:2409.09478

   Licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International licence
   (CC-BY-4.0). Note this differs from the Apache 2.0 licence covering the source
   code in this repository: the weights are CC-BY-4.0, the code is Apache 2.0.

   CHANGES MADE. The published checkpoints take two input channels (CT and PET).
   For use here they were widened to four by zero-padding the stem convolution's
   input dimension, adding two prompt channels that contribute nothing at
   initialisation; every trained weight is otherwise unchanged. The conversion is
   scripts/prepare_pretrained.py. CC-BY-4.0 requires such changes to be indicated,
   which this paragraph does.

   CC-BY-4.0 is not a copyleft licence: it permits adaptations to be released under
   different terms, so the weights trained here were free to carry any licence, with
   the attribution above retained.

   The weights trained here are published as:

      BS: Take the Hint -- Interactive Multitracer PET/CT Lesion Segmentation with a
      Scribble-Conditioned ResEnc U-Net
      Elmasry, A.; Sherif, M.; Ghazal, Y.; Elghotni, A.  Brightskies Inc.
      https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22176946   (version)
      https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22176945   (concept, newest version)

      Released under CC-BY-4.0 -- the same licence as the weights they were
      initialised from, and NOT the Apache 2.0 covering this repository's source.
